  "Number": 21,
  "Question": "For every \\(3^\\circ\\) rise in temperature, the volume of a certain gas expands by \\(4\\) cubic centimeters. If the volume of the gas is \\(24\\) cubic centimeters when the temperature is \\(32^\\circ,\\) what was the volume of the gas in cubic centimeters when the temperature was \\(20^\\circ?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\)",
    "B": "\\(12\\)",
    "C": "\\(15\\)",
    "D": "\\(16\\)",
    "E": "\\(40\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "From \\(20^\\circ\\) to \\(32^\\circ\\), the temperature rises by\n\\[\n32-20=12^\\circ.\n\\]\nThis contains \\(12\\div3=4\\) of the given \\(3^\\circ\\) increases. Each adds \\(4\\) cubic centimeters, so the volume increases by \\(4\\times4=16\\) cubic centimeters.\n\nThe volume at \\(20^\\circ\\) was therefore \\(24-16=\\boxed{8}\\) cubic centimeters, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
